    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6751\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the town law and the public officers\nlaw, in relation to the residency of the Wallkill comptroller\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 23 of the town law by adding a new\nsubdivision 28, providing that the person performing the functions of\ncomptroller in the Town of Wallkill, Orange County, need not be an\nelector of such town.\n\nSection 2: Amends section 3 of the public officers law by adding a new\nsubdivision 62, providing that the person holding the office of\ncomptroller of the Town of Wallkill, County of Orange, need not be a\nresident of such town, provided that the person resides within the\nCounty of Orange or an adjoining county within the state of New York.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was introduced at the request of the Town of Wallkill\nto fill the position of Town Comptroller\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
